<title>NORWAY: Saga secures first long-term UK oil deal.</title>
<headline>Saga secures first long-term UK oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saga Petroleum ASA said on Monday its British subsidiary, Saga UK, had concluded its first long-term sales contract for oil from the Forties and Brent fields on the British continental shelf.</p>
<p>Awarded to British Petroleum, the one year deal is worth almost one billion crowns.</p>
<p>BP had a similar contract with British-based Santa Fe Exploration, which Saga acquired at the end of last year.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
